//! Generated in-source native call contract reference.
//!
//! Registration/ABI, candidate naming, target recovery, and Rust implementation
//! are deliberately reported as separate facts. A third-party name or a Rust
//! match arm does not make a handler target-confirmed.
//! Arguments are listed in BP push order; native handlers pop them from the end.
//!
//! ## System group 0x80
//!
//! `0x80:0x00` `Sys80_00_Srand`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[seed: u32 seed]. BGI 1.622 sub_488820: srand(value) on the main thread's MSVC CRT state, shared with every native rand() caller (particles, Sys80:01/02).
//! `0x80:0x01` `Sys80_01_Rand`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_488840: pushes MSVC rand() (holdrand*214013+2531011, bits 16..30; initial seed 1).
//! `0x80:0x02` `Sys80_02_RandMax`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[max_exclusive: i32]. BGI 1.622 sub_488860: for n > 0 returns (((rand()<<8)^rand())<<8^rand()) % n with the three rand() calls in that order; n <= 0 returns 0 without calling rand().
//! `0x80:0x04` `Sys80_04_GetEngineTick`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_4888B0 -> sub_499290: wrapping 32-bit millisecond clock; host jumps backwards or over 500 ms (dword_503DE8) are excluded, and the value is frozen inside a pause section that froze it (deactivation with Sys81:68, modal dialogs). Interactive runs start at the host uptime, deterministic replays at 0.
//! `0x80:0x05` `Sys80_05_QueryPerformanceCounterNs`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[counter_out: BP pointer to u64]. BGI 1.622 sub_4888D0 -> sub_499430: QueryPerformanceCounter/frequency*1e9 as a u64 written low then high DWORD; returns 1. Not stopped by clock pauses; interactive runs read the host monotonic clock, replays derive it from the engine clock.
//! `0x80:0x06` `Sys80_06_SetPerformanceProfiling`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. BGI 1.622 sub_488900 -> sub_401600: stores the raw flag; non-zero resets count/total/within-budget/pending and sets the budget to 96% of one display refresh (sub_46F8E0, refresh rate dword_5177C8 or 60). Samples (sub_4017F0/sub_401830) time the update pass (sub_48D480, kept pending) plus scene composition before Present (sub_462010/sub_462050); Present and its vsync wait are not measured. Nanoseconds stand in for the QueryPerformanceCounter frequency; without a raster status (sub_45FBF0 failure) only the time test decides within-budget.
//! `0x80:0x07` `Sys80_07_ReadPerformanceMetric`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer to i32; metric_id: i32 enum 0..=3]. BGI 1.622 sub_488920 -> sub_401670 pops the metric then the output pointer: 0 sample count; 1 total/(freq*count)*1e6; 2 (budget>>1)*count/total*10000 when total > 0; 3 within^2/count^2*10000; other selectors and empty states write 0. x87 results are truncated through __int64 to a DWORD.
//! `0x80:0x08` `Sys80_08_ReadCursorPoint`: inputs=0, outputs=2, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_488950 -> sub_48F180: the active touch contact (dword_5666B0), else the cursor in client space mapped to game space by sub_45EE30 with (int) truncation; (0, 0) before the window exists; pushes x then y. Hosts deliver cursor positions already in game space; the target window cannot be resized (sub_461C40), the portable window can, with the same mapping.
//! `0x80:0x09` `Sys80_09_QueryPresentationState`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_488990 -> sub_460450 returns dword_565ED8, which sub_460460 sets to the engine clock (sub_499290) after a successful Present; 0 before the first frame.
//! `0x80:0x0A` `Sys80_0A_CopyGraphicsCapabilities`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer to 64-byte record]. BGI 1.622 sub_4889B0 copies 0x40 bytes from dword_518930 (.bss), which sub_46F100 fills at startup: [0] vendor index, [1] family (extended bits OR-ed in for 0/15), [2] model with extended model, [3] stepping, [4] brand byte (Intel) or CPUID 0x80000001 EBX word, [5]/[6]/[7] L1/L2/L3 words from the CPUID 2 descriptor table and CPUID 4 levels (Intel) or CPUID 0x80000005/6, [8] RDTSC MHz over one second, [9] processor count; a failed CPUID query returns early. Hosts without CPUID keep the zero record (cpu_record.rs).
//! `0x80:0x0B` `Sys80_0B_QueryGraphicsMemoryMetric`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_4889E0 -> sub_443540 returns CObjectManager+0x58, set by sub_46FB30 at startup (display mode 2) and on every display-mode change (sub_461670) from the processor record and that mode's size (dword_506B8C/dword_506BAC), in the target's 32-bit arithmetic.
//! `0x80:0x0C` `Sys80_0C_GetLocalTime`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer to SYSTEMTIME]. BGI 1.622 sub_488A00: GetLocalTime into the 16-byte SYSTEMTIME (year, month, weekday, day, hour, minute, second, ms), taken from one host time sample.
//! `0x80:0x0D` `Sys80_0D_GetPhysicalMemory`: inputs=0, outputs=2, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_488A20: GlobalMemoryStatus total then available physical bytes, each capped at 0x7FFFFFFF; pushes total, then available.
//! `0x80:0x0E` `Sys80_0E_QueryWindowMinimizeLatch`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_488AB0 -> sub_49ADB0 returns dword_566708: Sys80:65 sets it; WM_ACTIVATE clears it once the window is active and no longer iconic.
//! `0x80:0x0F` `Sys80_0F_QueryWindowActive`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_488AD0 -> sub_49ADA0: dword_5666FC, the last WM_ACTIVATE state.
//! `0x80:0x10` `Sys80_10_ResetInputConfiguration`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. BGI 1.622 sub_488AF0: stores the input-configuration flag (dword_506A44) and clears fields 0/1/2/4 of every input record (sub_46DF80); the field-3 accumulator read by Sys80:12 and field 5 survive.
//! `0x80:0x11` `Sys80_11_QueryKeyDown`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[descriptor: i32 target logical input descriptor]. BGI 1.622 sub_488B10 -> sub_46DAC0: bit 15 of GetAsyncKeyState for the logical key; with mouse mapping mode 1 (dword_566930) left reads left|right and right reads nothing; the system button swap is compensated; reports 0 unless the window is active or background polling (dword_566800) is on.
//! `0x80:0x12` `Sys80_12_SumInputDescriptorState`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[descriptors: pointer to linked/zero-terminated descriptor record]. BGI 1.622 sub_488B40: sums the field-3 accumulator (dword_518CB4[6*d], sub_46E1D0) over a zero-terminated contiguous DWORD array of descriptors; nothing is consumed.
//! `0x80:0x13` `Sys80_13_GetInputMessageSerial`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_488B80 -> sub_46EB20: dword_566850, incremented (sub_46EB10) by WM_CLOSE, every left/right/middle/X button down (before Knob capture), mouse wheel and horizontal wheel, and the press edges of WM_KEYDOWN, F10 and Alt.
//! `0x80:0x14` `Sys80_14_SetInputMasterGate`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[value: i32 configuration value]. BGI 1.622 sub_488BA0 -> sub_46DEE0: stores the skip-gate master flag dword_506A48 read by Sys80:17.
//! `0x80:0x15` `Sys80_15_SetInputLatchedState`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[value: i32 configuration value]. BGI 1.622 sub_488BC0 -> sub_46DEF0: stores the latched skip state dword_56683C read by Sys80:17.
//! `0x80:0x16` `Sys80_16_SampleConfiguredInput`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_488BE0 -> sub_46DF00: sets the poll flag dword_566840 and drains (sub_46E0A0) every descriptor of the 0x80000000 list dword_5069F8 (default {17}).
//! `0x80:0x17` `Sys80_17_QueryConfiguredInputGate`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_488BF0 -> sub_46E390: starting from the latched state, while the window is active and input configuration is on, walks dword_5069F8: a physically held key (sub_46DAC0) marks any-down; with the poll flag a draining hit latches, otherwise a held key returns at once; hits count only while the window is not minimized (dword_566700). The poll flag drops once nothing is held. Returns 1 when latched and the master gate (dword_506A48) is set.
//! `0x80:0x18` `Sys80_18_RegisterInputScope`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[scope: i32 input scope]. BGI 1.622 sub_488C10: packed = (scope<<16)|0xFFFF is inserted into the pointer chain as a whole-plane node (sub_46DC20, rect dword_506A4C) and into the keyboard chain (sub_46DC80), each before the first node whose scope is not greater, then one stateful sub_46E460 query whose result is discarded.
//! `0x80:0x19` `Sys80_19_QueryAndUnregisterInputScope`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[scope: i32 input scope]. BGI 1.622 sub_488C50: one stateful sub_46E460 query, then removes the first pointer-chain node (sub_46DD00) and keyboard-chain node (sub_46DD10) with that packed scope.
//! `0x80:0x1A` `Sys80_1A_QueryInputEventBits`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[scope: i32 registration scope]. BGI 1.622 sub_488C90 -> sub_46E460((scope<<16)|0xFFFF): when the keyboard chain accepts the scope (sub_46DD70: input on and scope >= the top keyboard node), the nineteen class tables (sub_46E1E0; each drains descriptors until one hits) and then the skip gate (sub_46E390, bit 31); when the pointer chain accepts it (sub_46DD90), descriptors 1/2/4/5/6 drain into bits 1/2/4/0x10/0x20.
//! `0x80:0x1B` `Sys80_1B_RegisterInputClassDescriptors`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[class_mask: i32 target input-class bit; descriptors: pointer to zero-terminated i32 array]. BGI 1.622 sub_488CC0 -> sub_46E500: pops the descriptor pointer, then the class; a list of 16 or more entries, then a class other than 0x40/0x80/0x100/0x200/0x1000/0x2000/0x4000/0x8000/0x40000000/0x80000000, is a script error; the zero-terminated list is copied into that fixed table (classes 0x100/0x200 are also the child lists of aggregate descriptors 193/194).
//! `0x80:0x1C` `Sys80_1C_QueryInputClassLevel`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[class_mask: i32 input-class mask]. BGI 1.622 sub_488D60 -> sub_46E5D0: wrapping sum of the field-3 accumulators of every descriptor in the selected class tables (1/2/4/0x10/0x20 and the nineteen classes; the 0x80000000 list is excluded).
//! `0x80:0x1D` `Sys80_1D_QueryScopedInputEvent`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[input_descriptor: i32 target logical input descriptor; scope: i32 registration scope]. BGI 1.622 sub_488D90 pops the descriptor, then the scope; descriptors 1/2 test the pointer chain (sub_46DD90), others the keyboard chain (sub_46DD70), and an accepted scope drains the descriptor (sub_46E0A0: lazy release, count, first-held bit 31).
//! `0x80:0x1E` `Sys80_1E_SetMouseButtonMappingMode`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[mode: i32 enum 0..=1]. BGI 1.622 sub_488DF0 -> sub_48F950: mode <= 1 (unsigned) is stored as the mouse mapping mode (dword_566930: 1 turns the right button into the left) and 1 is pushed; other values push 0.
//! `0x80:0x1F` `Sys80_1F_ConfigureCursorMotion`: inputs=6, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[cancel_on_large_move: bool/i32; updates_per_second: u32; duration_ms: u32 milliseconds; interpolation_mode: i32 enum; target_y: i32 logical pixels; target_x: i32 logical pixels]. BGI 1.622 sub_488E20 -> sub_48F280 (script order x, y, interpolation, duration, ups, cancel): ignored while iconic; steps = ups*duration/1000 (u32), at least 1; sub_48F430 then, each frame while the window is active, emits every step whose deadline start + duration*(step+1)/steps (u32) has passed, at start + sub_48F3D0(delta) (linear 16.16 or integer-angle cosine), the last step exactly at the target; with the cancel flag a cursor that moved more than ceil(presentation scale) from the last generated point stops it; an inactive window drops it.
//! `0x80:0x20` `Sys80_20_Alloc`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[size: u32 byte count]. Target 0x00488380 validates the requested size, allocates through sub_48DC70's memory-class table and raises the native VM error path when allocation returns zero.
//! `0x80:0x21` `Sys80_21_Free`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[pointer: opaque BP memory pointer]. Target 0x004883D0 treats null as success; non-null handles are decoded by sub_48DD10 and invalid/double-free values enter the native VM error path.
//! `0x80:0x24` `Sys80_24_CountFiles`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[pattern: Shift-JIS path pattern; recursive: bool/i32]. BGI 1.622 sub_488F50 -> sub_467110(no buffer, no limit): counts files matching the FindFirstFileA pattern (DOS wildcard rewriting, case-insensitive), then with the recursive flag every subdirectory's matches; recursion builds patterns from strrchr(pattern, '\\'), so a pattern without a backslash finds nothing below.
//! `0x80:0x25` `Sys80_25_EnumerateFiles`: inputs=5, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP byte-buffer pointer or null; capacity: i32 byte count; pattern: Shift-JIS path pattern; recursive: bool/i32; max_count: u32]. BGI 1.622 sub_488F90 (pops max count, recursive, pattern, capacity, buffer) -> sub_467110: matching files in NTFS order (upcased UTF-16), up to the count, packed as C strings, then each subdirectory recursively with prefix 'sub\\' and the remaining count (0 means unlimited, as the target's unsigned difference); a name that does not fit returns -1 after the earlier ones were copied; a null buffer returns the byte total, otherwise the count. No recursion without a backslash in the pattern.
//! `0x80:0x26` `Sys80_26_EnumerateDirectories`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP byte-buffer pointer or null; capacity: u32 byte count; pattern: Shift-JIS path pattern; max_count: u32]. BGI 1.622 sub_489010 -> sub_467460: immediate subdirectories other than . and .. in NTFS order, up to the count, packed as C strings; overflow returns -1; a null buffer returns the byte total, otherwise the count.
//! `0x80:0x27` `Sys80_27_MoveFile`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: Shift-JIS path; source: Shift-JIS path]. BGI 1.622 sub_489060: MoveFileA(last argument, first argument) without flags: fails when the destination exists (except a case-only rename), does not create its directory, moves files across volumes by copy and delete, directories only within a volume.
//! `0x80:0x28` `Sys80_28_CreateDirectory`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. BGI 1.622 sub_489090: CreateDirectoryA creates one level; an existing path or a missing parent fails.
//! `0x80:0x29` `Sys80_29_RemoveDirectory`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. BGI 1.622 sub_4890C0: RemoveDirectoryA removes an empty directory only.
//! `0x80:0x2A` `Sys80_2A_DirectoryExists`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. BGI 1.622 sub_4890F0: bit 4 (DIRECTORY) of GetFileAttributesA, 0 when the path does not exist.
//! `0x80:0x2B` `Sys80_2B_SplitPath`: inputs=5, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[drive_out: BP char buffer or null; directory_out: BP char buffer or null; filename_out: BP char buffer or null; extension_out: BP char buffer or null; source_path: Shift-JIS path or null]. BGI 1.622 sub_489130 pops the path, then the ext, name, dir and drive outputs; a non-null path is split as wide text (sub_42D7F0: MultiByteToWideChar(CP_ACP), _wsplitpath: drive 'X:', directory through the last '\\' or '/', name, extension from the last '.') and each non-null output receives its part; returns 1, or 0 without writes for a null path.
//! `0x80:0x2C` `Sys80_2C_GetFileAttributes`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. BGI 1.622 sub_4891A0: GetFileAttributesA unchanged (-1 when missing): READONLY from the host permission, DIRECTORY from the type, the other settable bits as stored by Sys80:2D (default ARCHIVE for files), NORMAL when nothing remains.
//! `0x80:0x2D` `Sys80_2D_SetFileAttributes`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[path: Shift-JIS path; attributes: u32 Win32 attribute mask]. BGI 1.622 sub_4891D0 pops the attribute mask, then the path: SetFileAttributesA keeps READONLY/HIDDEN/SYSTEM/ARCHIVE/TEMPORARY/OFFLINE/NOT_CONTENT_INDEXED (NORMAL alone clears them); READONLY maps to the host permission, the rest persists in an extended attribute.
//! `0x80:0x2F` `Sys80_2F_CopyFile`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: Shift-JIS path; source: Shift-JIS path]. BGI 1.622 sub_489200: clears READONLY on an existing destination (second-to-last argument), then CopyFileA(last argument, destination, FALSE): overwrite, data plus attributes (with ARCHIVE) and last-write time; a directory source fails.
//! `0x80:0x30` `Sys80_30_ReadFileBytes`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP byte-buffer pointer; archive_or_root: Shift-JIS string or null; file: Shift-JIS resource path]. BGI 1.622 sub_489250 -> sub_466010 (pops file, archive, destination): clears 16 bytes, reads the loose file below the primary root (then the Sys80:36/37 search directories), decoded by sub_465880 (DSC, CBG v1/v2, raw), else with a non-null archive the entry of primary_root+archive (composite archives search their members); a miss retries the media root and then goes to sub_465F80, which is a script error ('指定されたファイル [ a : f ] は存在しません') unless a media root exists (then the OK/Cancel media prompt loops); returns the decoded size, 0 for other archive errors. Without an archive the media root is tried for the loose file. See src/engine/resource_io.c.
//! `0x80:0x31` `Sys80_31_ReadFileRange`: inputs=5, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP byte-buffer pointer; secondary_root: Shift-JIS path or null; file: Shift-JIS resource path; offset: u32 byte offset; length: u32 byte count]. BGI 1.622 sub_489290 -> sub_466190 (pops length, offset, file, archive, destination): loose read under the primary root and search directories, then the media root (null archive) or primary_root+archive and media_root+archive; range per sub_465880 (both 0 = whole, count 0 or beyond the size 3, end beyond the size 2); returns 0, 1 missing, 2, 3, 5 read/decode failure, 6 over 64 MiB; never fatal.
//! `0x80:0x32` `Sys80_32_WriteFileBytes`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[path: Shift-JIS path; source: BP byte-buffer pointer; length: u32 byte count]. Target 0x004887F0 returns whether sub_465E30 wrote exactly the requested byte count.
//! `0x80:0x33` `Sys80_33_DeleteFile`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[root: Shift-JIS path or null; file: Shift-JIS relative path]. sub_488840 pops file, then root; it deletes root\\file, or primary root + file when the root is null (DeleteFileA), and pushes the success flag.
//! `0x80:0x34` `Sys80_34_FileExists`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[archive: Shift-JIS archive/root; file: Shift-JIS resource path]. BGI 1.622 sub_4893C0 -> sub_466B20 (pops file, then archive): with an archive, a loose non-directory below the primary root or search directories, else (names of 0x60+ bytes are fatal) the entry in primary_root+archive or media_root+archive; without, an absolute name is tested directly, otherwise the loose file below the primary or media root.
//! `0x80:0x35` `Sys80_35_FileSize`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[archive: Shift-JIS archive/root; file: Shift-JIS resource path]. BGI 1.622 sub_489400 -> sub_466840 (pops file, then archive): decoded size of the loose file, else of the archive entry (media root only after ARCHIVE_NOT_FOUND), else 0; without an archive the media root's loose file.
//! `0x80:0x36` `Sys80_36_SetAdditionalResourceSearch`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: boolean i32]. Target sub_465240 stores the value in dword_506BE0; it is a mode flag, not a commit operation.
//! `0x80:0x37` `Sys80_37_PrependResourceSearchPath`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. Target allocates a path node and prepends it to the linked list rooted at dword_566630.
//! `0x80:0x38` `Sys80_38_RegisterCompositeArchive`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS archive name; components: pointer to zero-terminated string-pointer array]. Target consumes a zero-terminated pointer array and constructs/registers a named DCArchiveComplex.
//! `0x80:0x39` `Sys80_39_SetValidatedFileRoot`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. Target accepts an existing directory and stores it with a trailing backslash in byte_518978.
//! `0x80:0x3A` `Sys80_3A_GetSpecialFolder`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP char buffer; mode: i32 enum 0..=5]. Target selects six Win32 system/shell folder sources, including ProgramFilesDir from the registry, and copies the resulting path.
//! `0x80:0x3B` `Sys80_3B_OpenFileDialog`: inputs=6, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[initial_directory: Shift-JIS path; description: Shift-JIS string; extension: Shift-JIS extension; destination: BP char buffer; title: Shift-JIS string; mode: i32 enum 0..=1]. Target builds one extension filter and calls GetOpenFileNameA/GetSaveFileNameA. The portable host now invokes a blocking native/scripted chooser on macOS, Windows and Linux while preserving target status codes.
//! `0x80:0x3C` `Sys80_3C_RequireResourceFile`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[file: Shift-JIS resource path; ignored_context: Shift-JIS string; message: Shift-JIS prompt text]. Target repeatedly searches configured roots and prompts Retry/Quit. The portable host performs the same loop through native macOS, Windows, or Linux message dialogs.
//! `0x80:0x3D` `Sys80_3D_GetConfiguredRoot`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP char buffer; kind: i32 enum 0..=1]. Target 0x00488B20/sub_4649A0 copies the primary root for kind 0, or the configured secondary root for kind 1; other values fail.
//! `0x80:0x3E` `Sys80_3E_SetPrimaryRoot`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[path: Shift-JIS path]. Target 0x00488B50 accepts only an existing directory, writes path plus a trailing backslash to the primary global root buffer and returns one.
//! `0x80:0x3F` `Sys80_3F_ConfigureRemovableArchive`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[archive_name: Shift-JIS marker/archive name; subdirectory: Shift-JIS relative directory; prompt: Shift-JIS prompt text; retry: boolean i32]. Target scans removable/CD drives for the configured archive marker and stores the successful drive/subdirectory as the secondary root. The portable host scans platform mount roots and preserves the retry loop.
//! `0x80:0x40` `Sys80_40_LoadProgramModule`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[archive: Shift-JIS archive; file: Shift-JIS BP filename]. sub_488C00 pops file then archive, decodes the module (sub_465AB0; a read/decode failure is fatal) and sub_444CE0 appends its code to the current CThread when it fits the code region (fatal otherwise). The value pushed is the code offset where the module starts (the previous code-used end). The target's disk-swap retry dialog for a missing archive is not reproduced; the portable runtime fails at once.
//! `0x80:0x41` `Sys80_41_FreeLastProgramModule`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[legacy_descriptor_slot: ignored ABI slot]. sub_488CD0 pops nothing. sub_444D80 unlinks the newest module record, rolls back the code-used end and pushes the remaining module count (the main program counts); with no record it pushes 0x80000001, and a remaining count of 0 is a fatal error.
//! `0x80:0x44` `Sys80_44_LoadProgramThread`: inputs=5, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[archive: Shift-JIS archive; file: Shift-JIS BP filename; operand_slots: i32 count; code_bytes: i32 byte count; data_bytes: i32 byte count]. sub_488D00 pops region p1, region p2, operand slots, file, archive. sub_48D080 reads the file (sub_465AB0; unreadable is fatal), appends a CThread at the end of the thread chain (sub_444A70 -> sub_4447C0: 4*slots operand bytes, p2 code region, p1 second region), loads the module into the code region (sub_444CE0; a module that does not fit is fatal) and returns the new thread id (CThread+8).
//! `0x80:0x45` `Sys80_45_RtcNoop`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. The release-image selector table points at __RTC_NumErrors, but the BP ABI exposes no output and no useful engine side effect.
//! `0x80:0x46` `Sys80_46_CurrentThreadId`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. Target sub_488D80 returns the current CThread field at +8.
//! `0x80:0x47` `Sys80_47_ThreadExists`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[thread_id: i32 CThread identifier]. Target recursively searches the CThread tree; identifier zero is never reported as present.
//! `0x80:0x48` `Sys80_48_EnqueueMessage`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[thread_or_program: thread/program handle; message: DWORD/BP value]. Target slot 0x00504420 calls BPThread_EnqueueDword and appends one value to CThread+0x5C/+0x60 FIFO state.
//! `0x80:0x49` `Sys80_49_DequeueMessage`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer to DWORD/value]. Target slot 0x00504424 calls BPThread_DequeueDword, writes one value through output_ptr, and reports whether a value was available.
//! `0x80:0x4A` `Sys80_4A_EnqueueMessageArray`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[thread_or_program: thread/program handle; message_count: i32 count; messages_ptr: BP pointer to DWORD/value array]. Target handler appends an array by repeatedly invoking the confirmed one-value FIFO enqueue helper.
//! `0x80:0x4B` `Sys80_4B_DequeueMessageArray`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[max_count: i32 count; output_ptr: BP pointer to DWORD/value array]. Target handler performs bounded FIFO dequeue and returns the number written to output_ptr.
//! `0x80:0x4C` `Sys80_4C_InvokeThreadCallback`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[thread_or_program: thread/program handle; arg1: DWORD/BP value; arg2: DWORD/BP value; arg3: DWORD/BP value]. sub_488FC0: finds the thread with sub_444B90 (id 0, the empty root CThread, is never found; the script thread is 1) and queues {a, b, c} on its current procedure (sub_445230 -> sub_431B40); pushes 1 when queued, 0 for an unknown thread or no procedure.
//! `0x80:0x50` `Sys80_50_SetSystemWaitState`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[value: i32 global system state]. Target 0x00489030 pops one i32 and sub_4319B0 stores it unchanged in dword_507688. The native C return value 1 is not a BP stack output.
//! `0x80:0x52` `Sys80_52_SetMainLoopWaitOverride`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[value: i32]. Target handler 0x00489050 leaves the popped i32 in EAX and sub_48D1B0 stores it in dword_503EF8; sub_48D1C0 is consumed by the executable main-loop pacing branch.
//! `0x80:0x53` `Sys80_53_ArmNextBinaryAsync`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. Target handler 0x00489070 stores one in dword_5668A0. Sys81:30 and Graph90:F6 consume and reset this one-shot flag when selecting DCProcReadBinary or DCProcDecodeBMV.
//! `0x80:0x54` `WaitWndMsg`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[arg0: unrecovered BP value]. Target sub_489080 pops the message id, allocates 0x24 bytes, constructs CProcWaitWndMsg through sub_43D4D0, and registers the waiter through sub_499F40. The virtual poll consumes the matching signaled waiter and pushes lParam followed by wParam.
//! `0x80:0x58` `SetThreadTimer`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[arg0: unrecovered BP value]. BGI 1.622 sub_489C00 -> sub_445660: CThread+0x84 = sub_499290() + duration with 32-bit wrap (negative durations are not clamped).
//! `0x80:0x59` `Sys80_59_SetAndQueryThreadTimer`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[duration_ms: i32 milliseconds]. BGI 1.622 sub_489C20: CThread+0x84 += duration (sub_445680), then pushes whether sub_445630 (signed deadline - now, 0 when not positive) is non-zero.
//! `0x80:0x5A` `WaitTiming`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_489C60: remaining = sub_445630 (signed CThread+0x84 - now, 0 when not positive); a positive value installs CProcWaitTiming with deadline now + remaining (unsigned completion test deadline <= now, sub_431E30); pushes remaining != 0 and returns status 2.
//! `0x80:0x5C` `WaitTimingOrInput`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[duration_ms: i32 milliseconds; input_enabled: bool/i32; input_scope: i32 mask]. Target sub_4891F0 pops scope, input flag, duration and installs CProcWaitTimingEx (sub_43D2E0): deadline = engine tick + duration in the procedure (not the 0x80:0x5A thread timer); with input enabled the packed scope is registered like 0x80:0x18 and primed. Tick sub_43D430 pushes 0 on deadline, cleared dword_507688, callback code 0 or 1, and 1 on input bits & (dword_507690|0x80000181); the destructor unregisters the scope.
//! `0x80:0x5D` `Sys80_5D_SetExclusiveThread`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target handler 0x00489290 stores either the current CThread pointer or null through sub_48D170 and mirrors whether exclusive scheduling is enabled.
//! `0x80:0x5E` `Sys80_5E_SwitchThread`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=SwitchCoroutine, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[program: program/thread handle]. sub_4892B0 stores the thread id and returns 3; the scheduler (sub_48CD70) runs that thread next in the same pass and continues from its successor, and an unknown id (0 included) ends the pass.
//! `0x80:0x5F` `Sys80_5F_Yield`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Yield, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. Target sub_4892D0 returns native interpreter status 1 without BP stack or CThread state changes. The outer interpreter ends the current cooperative pass and resumes at the next instruction.
//! `0x80:0x60` `Sys80_60_ConfigureDisplayMode`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[mode: i32 display mode 0..=7; adapter: i32 adapter 0..=1; fullscreen: bool/i32]. Target handler 0x004892E0 pops fullscreen, adapter, then mode and calls sub_461110(mode, adapter, fullscreen); adapter>=2 or mode>=8 is fatal.
//! `0x80:0x61` `Sys80_61_QueryFullscreen`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[]. Target handler 0x00489340 pushes sub_45F640(), the current fullscreen state.
//! `0x80:0x62` `Sys80_62_ConfigureFullscreenHotkeys`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32; descriptor_list: BP pointer to zero-terminated i32 list]. Target handler 0x00489360 passes an enable flag and zero-terminated descriptor list to sub_461740. The list may contain at most fifteen nonzero entries.
//! `0x80:0x63` `Sys80_63_SetAspectPreservingScaling`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target handler 0x004893A0 calls sub_45E860(argument==0): zero selects stretch mode 1; nonzero selects aspect-preserving fit mode 0.
//! `0x80:0x64` `Sys80_64_SetWindowVisible`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target handler 0x004893C0 calls sub_49A170 and then clears transient input state through sub_46DA20.
//! `0x80:0x65` `Sys80_65_MinimizeWindow`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_489ED0: CloseWindow(hWndParent), clears the transient input records (sub_46DF80) and sets the minimize latch dword_566708.
//! `0x80:0x66` `Sys80_66_SetWindowTitle`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[text: Shift-JIS string]. Target handler 0x00489400 calls SetWindowTextA and persists the title in the engine's 256-byte title buffer on success.
//! `0x80:0x67` `Sys80_67_SetCursorIndex`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[cursor_index: i32 enum 0..=4]. Target handler 0x00489430 validates 0..=4 and stores the index used by WM_SETCURSOR.
//! `0x80:0x68` `Sys80_68_SetNativeCloseMode`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target sub_49A0D0 stores the value and updates SC_CLOSE. Zero intercepts WM_CLOSE into an engine event; nonzero permits native close processing.
//! `0x80:0x69` `Sys80_69_RequestWindowClose`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. Target handler 0x004894B0 calls PostMessageA(hWndParent, WM_CLOSE, 0, 0). Portable frontends defer the request until the current scheduler pass returns, then run the same Sys80:68 close-mode gate: mode 0 queues native event `[2,0,0]` for sysmsg._bp, while nonzero allows host-window termination.
//! `0x80:0x6A` `Sys80_6A_TerminateInterpreter`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=TerminateInterpreter, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[]. Target handler returns native interpreter status 6. The outer runtime treats this as interpreter termination; it is not a resumable cooperative yield.
//! `0x80:0x6B` `Sys80_6B_SelectBootstrap`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=SwitchCoroutine, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[root_or_archive_path: Shift-JIS path; archive_namespace: Shift-JIS string]. Target handler 0x004894E0 configures the primary root/archive pair through sub_4650F0 and returns interpreter status 5 to re-enter bootstrap selection.
//! `0x80:0x6C` `Sys80_6C_SetFileDropEnabled`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target sub_463A80 stores the flag, calls DragAcceptFiles and clears the pending dropped-file buffer.
//! `0x80:0x6D` `Sys80_6D_QueryDroppedFile`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP char buffer]. Target sub_463AE0 copies the pending dropped path and returns one when enabled and nonempty. Querying does not clear the native buffer.
//! `0x80:0x6E` `Sys80_6E_SetRasterWaitEnabled`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target handler 0x00489560 stores the raw value in dword_507220, which gates the raster/vblank wait path.
//! `0x80:0x6F` `Sys80_6F_QueryDisplayAspectMismatch`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[]. Target sub_461550 compares the desktop aspect ratio with the configured game/base aspect after scaling both by 10000.
//! `0x80:0x70` `Sys80_70_AllocateGlobalConfig`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[shift: i32 0..=12]. Target handler validates shift<=12, allocates 4096<<shift bytes, frees the previous buffer and zero-fills the replacement.
//! `0x80:0x71` `Sys80_71_ClearGlobalConfig`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. Target handler zeroes exactly the currently allocated global-config byte count.
//! `0x80:0x74` `Sys80_74_SetSaveDataIntegrity`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: bool/i32]. Target handler stores the raw integer in dword_506BDC. Zero alone disables save-slot encryption/checking.
//! `0x80:0x78` `Sys80_78_SaveConfigSlot`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[slot: i32; label: Shift-JIS string shorter than 40 bytes]. Target writes BGI%04d.cad as a 64-byte SYSTEMTIME/label header followed by the whole global-config buffer. Labels of 40 bytes or more are fatal.
//! `0x80:0x79` `Sys80_79_LoadConfigSlot`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[slot: i32]. Target loads and optionally decrypts the slot, applies its payload, then restores the first 1024 global-config bytes. Status: 0 success, 1 missing/empty, 2 wrong length, 3 integrity failure.
//! `0x80:0x7A` `Sys80_7A_ReadConfigSlotHeader`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP pointer to 64 bytes; slot: i32]. Target copies the first 64 bytes only when the file length equals 64 plus the current global-config size. Status: 0 success, 1 missing/empty, 2 partial or wrong length.
//! `0x80:0x7B` `Sys80_7B_ValidateConfigSlot`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[slot: i32]. Target reads and optionally verifies/decrypts the complete slot without applying the payload. Status codes match Sys80_79.
//! `0x80:0x80` `Sys80_80_LoadGlobalUserData`: inputs=0, outputs=3, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[]. Target loads BGI.gdb, decodes SDC data and maps missing/decode failures to status 1/2.
//! `0x80:0x81` `Sys80_81_SaveGlobalUserData`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[]. Target writes the BURIKO GDB 3.00 header, global data, resource names and read-flag tables to BGI.gdb.
//! `0x80:0x82` `Sys80_82_WriteGlobalDataBlock`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[offset: i32 byte offset; buffer: BP pointer; length: i32 byte count]. Target copies into the fixed 1 MiB global data region and treats zero/out-of-range transfers as fatal.
//! `0x80:0x83` `Sys80_83_ReadGlobalDataBlock`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[offset: i32 byte offset; buffer: BP pointer; length: i32 byte count]. Target copies from the fixed 1 MiB global data region and treats zero/out-of-range transfers as fatal.
//! `0x80:0x84` `Sys80_84_InternResourceName`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string]. Target handler 0x004899B0 calls sub_46B430, which interns the name and then returns one. The table's stable index remains internal and is not returned to BP code.
//! `0x80:0x85` `Sys80_85_ResourceNameExists`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string]. Target handler 0x004899E0 performs lookup only and must not insert missing names.
//! `0x80:0x88` `Sys80_88_CreateOrResizeReadFlagTable`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; bit_count: i32 bit count]. Target handler 0x00489A10 calls ReadFlagTable_CreateOrResize. It is not a scenario-code preprocessing syscall.
//! `0x80:0x89` `Sys80_89_SetReadFlagBit`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; bit_offset: i32 bit index; enabled: bool/i32]. Target handler 0x00489A40 changes one bit in a named compact bitset.
//! `0x80:0x8A` `Sys80_8A_SetReadFlagRange`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; start_bit: i32 bit index; enabled: bool/i32; bit_count: i32 bit count]. Target handler 0x00489AC0 calls ReadFlagTable_SetRange at 0x00446D40 and validates the complete range.
//! `0x80:0x8B` `Sys80_8B_QueryReadFlagBit`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; output_ptr: BP pointer to i32; bit_offset: i32 bit index]. Target handler 0x00489B80 writes the queried bit through a BP pointer and returns a separate status.
//! `0x80:0x90` `Sys80_90_ResetStructuredHistory`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[capacity: i32 record count]. Frees all native 0x40-byte history nodes, clears head/tail/count and stores the new capacity.
//! `0x80:0x91` `Sys80_91_StructuredHistoryCount`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. Returns the process-global bounded history count.
//! `0x80:0x94` `Sys80_94_AppendStructuredHistoryFields`: inputs=13, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[value0: i32; value1: i32; value2: i32; value3: i32; value4: i32; value5: i32; value6: i32; value7: i32; value8: i32; short_text1: Shift-JIS string; short_text2: Shift-JIS string; short_text3: Shift-JIS string; text: Shift-JIS string]. Allocates a native history node, validates 31/255-byte string limits, appends at the tail and evicts the oldest record at capacity.
//! `0x80:0x95` `Sys80_95_ReadStructuredHistory`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer to record; newest_index: u32 index]. Index zero selects the newest record; writes the target record layout without the extended field.
//! `0x80:0x96` `Sys80_96_AppendStructuredHistoryRecord`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[record_ptr: BP pointer to record]. Imports the target scalar/string record layout, including the optional extended text at byte 512.
//! `0x80:0x97` `Sys80_97_ReadStructuredHistoryExtended`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer to record; newest_index: u32 index]. Same newest-first lookup as 0x95 and additionally copies the optional extended text.
//! `0x80:0x98` `Sys80_98_IndexedRecordOpen`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle_output: BP pointer to i32; capacity: u32 record count; record_size: u32 byte count]. Creates a capacity-bounded fixed-record table and writes a monotonically allocated integer identifier.
//! `0x80:0x99` `Sys80_99_IndexedRecordClose`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: i32 table identifier]. Closes an indexed-record table; missing identifiers return one.
//! `0x80:0x9A` `Sys80_9A_IndexedRecordCount`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer to i32; handle: i32 table identifier]. Writes the current record count through the output pointer.
//! `0x80:0x9C` `Sys80_9C_IndexedRecordPush`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: i32 table identifier; source: BP pointer]. Copies one fixed-size record to the front and truncates records beyond capacity.
//! `0x80:0x9D` `Sys80_9D_IndexedRecordLoad`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer; handle: i32 table identifier; index: u32 newest-first index]. Loads one newest-first record; missing table is one and invalid index is two.
//! `0x80:0x9E` `Sys80_9E_IndexedRecordRemove`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: i32 table identifier; start: u32 newest-first index; count: u32 record count]. Removes up to count records starting at a newest-first index.
//! `0x80:0xA0` `Sys80_A0_PollQueuedEvent`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[output_ptr: BP pointer to three i32 values]. Pops the oldest process-global three-DWORD event into caller memory.
//! `0x80:0xA1` `Sys80_A1_PostQueuedEvent`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[event_code: i32; parameter: i32]. Queues [0,event_code,parameter] in the target critical-section protected FIFO.
//! `0x80:0xA8` `Sys80_A8_SetRegisteredObjectState`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object_id: i32 registry identifier; state: i32]. sub_48A1B0: writes DCIndProc+0x10 (the enabled flag, 1 at construction) of the registered processor and pushes whether the handle exists. Processors with 0 are skipped by the per-frame update and drain no messages.
//! `0x80:0xA9` `Sys80_A9_GetRegisteredObjectState`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object_id: i32 registry identifier; output_ptr: BP pointer to i32]. sub_48A200: pops the output pointer then the handle, writes DCIndProc+0x10 and pushes whether the handle exists.
//! `0x80:0xAC` `Sys80_AC_QueueRegisteredObjectMessage`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[object_id: i32 registry identifier; count: i32 DWORD count 1..=256; descriptor: BP pointer to DWORD array]. sub_48A250: queues a 1..256-word message on the registered processor (other counts queue nothing) and pushes whether the handle exists. Each frame enabled processors drain their queue newest-registration first: [0, v] sets the enabled flag, other messages go to sub_44A250 (activate, select group/item, pointer processing, item bitmaps, item depth/position).
//! `0x80:0xAF` `Sys80_AF_SetSystemModeFlag`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[mode: i32 0..=1]. Accepts only zero or one and stores the process-global mode queried by the System81 extension.
//! `0x80:0xB0` `Sys80_B0_CreateExclusionSection`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; capacity: i32]. Creates a named capacity-limited CExclusion section; duplicate names return zero.
//! `0x80:0xB1` `Sys80_B1_DeleteExclusionSection`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string]. Returns 0x80000001 when missing and 0x80000002 while holders or waiters remain.
//! `0x80:0xB4` `Sys80_B4_WaitExclusionSection`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; priority: u32]. Installs CProcExclusion, queues the current thread by descending priority and resumes only when it is queue head and capacity is available.
//! `0x80:0xB5` `Sys80_B5_LeaveExclusionSection`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string]. Releases one holder entry for the current thread; missing/not-owner map to 0x80000001/0x80000003.
//! `0x80:0xB6` `Sys80_B6_QueryExclusionSection`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[name: Shift-JIS string; priority: u32]. Returns zero when capacity covers current holders plus all queued priorities greater than or equal to the request, otherwise 0x80000004.
//! `0x80:0xC0` `Sys80_C0_EncodeData`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP pointer; source: BP pointer; length: u32 bytes]. Target handler constructs CProcEncodeData from destination, source, and length; completion publishes the encoded length.
//! `0x80:0xC1` `Sys80_C1_DecodeSdcBuffer`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer; source: BP pointer]. Exact 0x0048A4D0 saves the first native pop in ESI and passes it in EAX as the SDC source to sub_4938F0; the second pop is its destination argument.
//! `0x80:0xC4` `Sys80_C4_EncodeStructArray`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP pointer; source: BP pointer; record_size: u32 bytes; record_count: u32]. Target handler constructs CProcEncodeStruct, applying DCFS record transform and SDC compression asynchronously.
//! `0x80:0xC5` `Sys80_C5_DecodeStructArray`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer; source: BP pointer]. Target handler synchronously performs SDC decompression followed by DCFS reconstruction and returns the record count.
//! `0x80:0xCF` `Sys80_CF_DecodeData`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=yes, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=WaitProcedure, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[destination: BP pointer; source: BP pointer; requested_length: u32 bytes]. BGI 1.622 499120/465880: SDC, DSC, native CBG v1/v2 buffer or raw copy; input length is not decoded capacity. Tagged BP addresses are resolved; invalid decode returns zero.
//! `0x80:0xD0` `Sys80_D0_RecordTableOpen`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle_out: BP pointer to i32; record_size: i32 bytes]. Target allocates an integer-handle keyed table whose entries are separately allocated record nodes; there is no fixed table capacity. Record sizes <=1 return 0x80000001.
//! `0x80:0xD1` `Sys80_D1_RecordTableClose`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: integer handle]. Target removes the integer-handle table; a missing table returns 0x80000002.
//! `0x80:0xD2` `Sys80_D2_RecordTableInsert`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: integer handle; key: Shift-JIS string; source: BP pointer]. Target inserts a separately allocated fixed-size record node or replaces the existing node selected by string key.
//! `0x80:0xD3` `Sys80_D3_RecordTableRemove`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[handle: integer handle; key: Shift-JIS string]. Target distinguishes missing table from missing key.
//! `0x80:0xD4` `Sys80_D4_RecordTableFetch`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer; handle: integer handle; key: nullable Shift-JIS pointer; index: i32]. Target fetches by key or linked-list insertion-order index and copies the fixed-size record.
//! `0x80:0xD8` `Sys80_D8_ClearStringNamespaces`: inputs=0, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. Target clears all string namespaces except protected table id 0x80000000.
//! `0x80:0xD9` `Sys80_D9_StringNamespaceCount`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[table_id: i32]. Target returns the number of interned strings in one namespace.
//! `0x80:0xDA` `Sys80_DA_ReplaceStringNamespace`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[table_id: i32; count: i32; source: BP pointer]. Target replaces a namespace from a packed string sequence or removes it when count is zero.
//! `0x80:0xDB` `Sys80_DB_SerializeStringNamespace`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: nullable BP pointer; table_id: i32]. Target serializes one namespace including each NUL terminator.
//! `0x80:0xDC` `Sys80_DC_InternStringNamespace`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[table_id: i32; value: Shift-JIS string]. Target interns/appends a string in one namespace with no graph-resource side effect.
//! `0x80:0xDD` `Sys80_DD_CopyIndexedNamespaceEntry`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer to byte buffer; table_id: i32 namespace identifier; index: i32 record index]. Target handler 0x0048A900 passes destination/table/index to sub_495850. The helper locates the 12-byte metadata slot, then copies the entry payload pointer by its stored byte length; sub_495550 constructs those payloads as Shift-JIS strings including the terminating NUL. Missing table/index map to 0x80000001/0x80000002.
//! `0x80:0xDE` `Sys80_DE_StringNamespaceEntryLength`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[length_out: BP pointer to i32; table_id: i32; index: i32]. Target reports the encoded byte length of one namespace entry without copying it.
//! `0x80:0xE0` `Sys80_E0_LaunchProcessWait`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[working_directory: Shift-JIS string; command_line: Shift-JIS string; error_message: Shift-JIS string; restore_parent: bool/i32]. Target launches a process, waits for it, and optionally restores the parent window.
//! `0x80:0xE1` `Sys80_E1_RestartWithCommand`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=TerminateInterpreter, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[working_directory: nullable Shift-JIS pointer; command_line: non-null Shift-JIS pointer; error_message: nullable Shift-JIS pointer]. Target accepts nullable working/error pointers, requires a non-null command pointer, stores restart fields, destroys the main window, returns native control status 6, and launches after WinMain cleanup.
//! `0x80:0xE2` `Sys80_E2_LaunchProcessWaitUninstaller`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[working_directory: Shift-JIS string; command_line: Shift-JIS string; error_message: Shift-JIS string]. Target launches and waits, then additionally waits for the named uninstaller synchronization object.
//! `0x80:0xE3` `Sys80_E3_ShellOpen`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[target: Shift-JIS string]. Target invokes ShellExecute with the open verb.
//! `0x80:0xE8` `Sys80_E8_WriteGameId`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: BP pointer]. Target writes the literal Tayutama2TV string.
//! `0x80:0xE9` `Sys80_E9_HashFile`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[hash_out: BP pointer to 8 bytes; path: Shift-JIS string]. Target hashes bytes with h=byte+233*h and four rolling tail accumulators.
//! `0x80:0xEA` `Sys80_EA_SetUninstallerProduct`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[product: Shift-JIS string]. Target formats and stores the mutex name `Uninstaller for <product> is executing.` used by the uninstaller wait loop.
//! `0x80:0xF0` `Sys80_F0_ShowInputDialog`: inputs=8, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[initial_text: Shift-JIS string; output_value1: BP pointer to i32; output_value2: BP pointer to i32; output_text: BP character buffer; option_value1: i32; option_value2: i32; mode: i32; caption: Shift-JIS string]. Target sub_471FB0 edits one Shift-JIS buffer plus two DWORD options. VM mediation now preserves all three output writes while the host supplies a cross-platform modal editor.
//! `0x80:0xF1` `Sys80_F1_ShowInstallerDialog`: inputs=6, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[text1: Shift-JIS string; text2: nullable Shift-JIS string; text3: Shift-JIS string; text4: Shift-JIS string; mode1: i32; mode2: i32]. Target sub_472050 opens one of two installer dialog resources using four text fields and two mode globals. Portable hosts expose the same modal success/cancel boundary.
//! `0x80:0xF2` `Sys80_F2_RunInstallerWorkflow`: inputs=14, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[root: Shift-JIS installation path; optional_directories: nullable zero-terminated string-pointer list; required_directories: zero-terminated string-pointer list; file_count: i32; metadata: Shift-JIS string/pointer; source_files: pointer to file_count Shift-JIS pointers; destination_files: pointer to file_count Shift-JIS pointers; flags: i32; format_string: Shift-JIS string; vendor: Shift-JIS string; product: Shift-JIS string; uninstall_source: nullable Shift-JIS string; prompt: Shift-JIS string; mode: i32]. Target sub_472150 creates the installation tree, copies parallel file lists, writes uninst.lst and InstalledFolder metadata. The portable host performs those operations without Win32-only dialog/resource internals.
//! `0x80:0xF3` `Sys80_F3_RunShortcutInstallerWorkflow`: inputs=8, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[target_root: Shift-JIS path; primary_target: Shift-JIS relative path; primary_shortcut_name: Shift-JIS string; secondary_target: Shift-JIS relative path; secondary_shortcut_name: Shift-JIS string; program_group: Shift-JIS string; create_program_group: bool/i32; create_desktop: bool/i32]. Target sub_471530 creates the primary desktop shortcut and up to two program-menu shortcuts from one target root and two relative targets. Portable hosts preserve the same branching and file destinations.
//! `0x80:0xF4` `Sys80_F4_RemoveUninstallListedFiles`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[root: Shift-JIS path; exclusions: pointer to NUL-terminated string-pointer array]. Target reads raw LF-separated Shift-JIS entries from root\\uninst.lst and deletes each except leading-@ directives, exact `uninst.lst`, and byte-exact exclusions.
//! `0x80:0xF5` `Sys80_F5_AppendUninstallListEntries`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[root: Shift-JIS path; entries: pointer to NUL-terminated string-pointer array]. Target requires root\\uninst.lst to exist, appends entries absent by C-string substring search, and rewrites the terminal NUL.
//! `0x80:0xF6` `Sys80_F6_RemoveInstallerShortcuts`: inputs=4, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[file_name: Shift-JIS string; secondary_file: Shift-JIS string; program_group: Shift-JIS string; remove_group: bool/i32]. Target removes desktop/program-menu shortcuts and optionally the group.
//! `0x80:0xF7` `Sys80_F7_CreateShortcut`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[program_group: nullable Shift-JIS string; shortcut_name: Shift-JIS string; target: Shift-JIS string]. Target passes ECX=0 to sub_4713F0: null group writes the desktop, non-null group writes CSIDL_PROGRAMS\\group. Hosts create .lnk on Windows and executable desktop-compatible launchers elsewhere.
//! `0x80:0xF8` `Sys80_F8_ReadInstalledFolder`: inputs=3, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[output: BP character buffer; vendor: Shift-JIS string; product: Shift-JIS string]. Target reads HKLM Software\\vendor\\product InstalledFolder. Windows reads the native registry and all hosts fall back to the persistent platform store.
//! `0x80:0xF9` `Sys80_F9_DeleteInstalledRegistryKey`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[vendor: Shift-JIS string; product: Shift-JIS string]. Target deletes HKLM Software\\vendor\\product.
//! `0x80:0xFA` `Sys80_FA_ReadWindowsPathFile`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[output: BP character buffer; file_name: Shift-JIS string]. Target reads WindowsDir\\file and accepts only NUL-terminated content ending in a backslash before the terminator.
//! `0x80:0xFB` `Sys80_FB_WriteWindowsDirectory`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[output: BP character buffer]. Target calls sub_467570 with selector zero and writes the resulting directory. The VM writes the host special-folder result through the exact BP pointer contract.
//! `0x80:0xFC` `Sys80_FC_RegisterFileAssociation`: inputs=5, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[extension: Shift-JIS string; class_name: Shift-JIS string; description: Shift-JIS string; icon: Shift-JIS string; open_command: Shift-JIS string]. Target writes the extension/class/description/icon/open-command hierarchy under HKCR. Windows writes HKCU\\Software\\Classes; all hosts persist the equivalent association in the platform store.
//! `0x80:0xFD` `Sys80_FD_QueryLauncherMode`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=Partial; params=[]. Target returns the launcher-mode global established by startup. The portable runtime returns the configured launcher mode through SysApi instead of forcing a constant fallback.
//! `0x80:0xFE` `Sys80_FE_InstallerFeatureAvailable`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. Target handler pushes constant 1.
//!
//! ## System extended group 0x81
//!
//! `0x81:0x04` `Sys81_04_SetClockJumpThreshold`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[threshold_ms: i32 milliseconds]. BGI 1.622 sub_48BE20 -> sub_499390: 50..=60000 sets dword_503DE8 (initially 500), the jump sub_499290 treats as a pause.
//! `0x81:0x07` `Sys81_07_CopyCoordinateSlot`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[index: i32; destination: pointer to two i32]. sub_48BE50 -> sub_48F090: index < 5 copies dword_503E40[index], the logical point of the last press of left/right/middle/X1/X2 (WndProc sub_48F060), (-1, -1) before any.
//! `0x81:0x08` `Sys81_08_GetUserName`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: Shift-JIS buffer]. sub_48BE80: GetUserNameA into a 257-byte buffer; a longer name leaves it unchanged.
//! `0x81:0x09` `Sys81_09_GetComputerName`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: Shift-JIS buffer]. sub_48BEB0: GetComputerNameA with nSize 16 (NetBIOS name: host name's first label, upper case, 15 chars).
//! `0x81:0x0A` `Sys81_0A_GetCpuBrand`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: Shift-JIS buffer]. sub_48BEE0 -> sub_46FC80: CPUID brand string through sub_496650 space folding; 0 without leaf 0x80000004 (no CPUID host).
//! `0x81:0x0B` `Sys81_0B_GetCpuDisplayInfo`: inputs=3, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[reserved: pointer; signature: pointer to four i32; text: Shift-JIS buffer]. sub_48BF10 -> sub_45E9F0: D3DADAPTER_IDENTIFIER9 Description (renderer adapter name) through sub_496650 and the DriverVersion words; first argument ignored.
//! `0x81:0x0C` `Sys81_0C_GetOsVersion`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[service_pack: Shift-JIS buffer; version: pointer to four u32]. sub_48BF40 -> sub_46FD60: GetVersionExA major/minor/build/platform and szCSDVersion; zeroed structure without Windows.
//! `0x81:0x0D` `Sys81_0D_GetPhysicalMemoryMb`: inputs=2, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[available_mb: pointer to u32; total_mb: pointer to u32]. sub_48BFD0: GlobalMemoryStatusEx total/available physical memory >> 20.
//! `0x81:0x0E` `Sys81_0E_GetAdjustedDesktopDimensions`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: pointer to two u32]. sub_48C060 -> sub_45EAE0(.., 1): start-up desktop mode, halved for side-by-side (>= 2.5:1) or stacked (<= 1.25:1) monitors, unsigned.
//! `0x81:0x0F` `Sys81_0F_IsMainWindowMinimized`: inputs=0, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[]. BGI 1.622 sub_48C080 pushes IsIconic(hWndParent); the window frontend refreshes the iconic state every frame and on focus changes.
//! `0x81:0x10` `Sys81_10_SwapInputBinding`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[replacement: i32; index: i32]. sub_48C0A0 -> sub_46DFA0: swaps the per-key repeat flag of a virtual key; >= 0x100 is fatal (不正な仮想キーコード).
//! `0x81:0x11` `Sys81_11_CopyKeyboardState`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: pointer to 256 bytes]. sub_48C0E0: GetKeyboardState (0x80 held, bit 0 toggled per press).
//! `0x81:0x14` `Sys81_14_SetKeyboardPollingOverride`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: i32]. sub_48C100 -> sub_46DAA0: dword_566800 background key polling.
//! `0x81:0x16` `Sys81_16_ConfigurePointerHistory`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[distance: i32; capacity: i32]. sub_48C120 -> sub_46B720: touch history capacity <= 0x200 and minimum step; empties the history.
//! `0x81:0x17` `Sys81_17_CopyPointerHistory`: inputs=4, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[count: i32; start: i32; distances: pointer to i32 array; points: pointer to x/y pairs]. sub_48C160 -> sub_46B860: WM_TOUCH history walk; the host delivers no WM_TOUCH, so 0.
//! `0x81:0x18` `Sys81_18_RegisterTouchInput`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[enabled: i32]. sub_48C1B0 -> sub_46B660: RegisterTouchWindow when available; 0 on hosts without touch windows.
//! `0x81:0x19` `Sys81_19_CopyTouchRecords`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: pointer to six-DWORD records]. sub_48C1E0 -> sub_46B6A0: active touch contacts (none without WM_TOUCH).
//! `0x81:0x1B` `Sys81_1B_SetControllerWakeEntry`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[value: i32; index: i32]. sub_48C210 -> sub_4613A0: index < 0x24 stores dword_565F20[index].
//! `0x81:0x1D` `Sys81_1D_QueryControllerState`: inputs=2, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[destination: pointer to six i32; device: pointer/nullable device selector]. sub_48C250 -> sub_4613C0: DirectInput joystick sum; no DirectInput devices on the host, so 0 and nothing written.
//! `0x81:0x1E` `Sys81_1E_InjectMouseClick`: inputs=1, outputs=1, procedure=no, raw_bit8=yes, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[button_code: i32]. sub_48C290 -> sub_46EB30: SendMessageA down/up for buttons 1/2/4/5/6 at the GetCursorPos point (screen coordinates read as client ones).
//! `0x81:0x1F` `Sys81_1F_SetMessageAuxiliaryInputMask`: inputs=1, outputs=0, procedure=no, raw_bit8=no, scheduling=Continue, recovery=TargetConfirmed, implementation=PortableEquivalent; params=[mask: i32 bit mask]. sub_48C2C0 -> sub_431DC0: dword_507690 (initially 0x2000), the extra input bits of CProcDspMsg/CProcedure.
